      ],
      "body": "The currently admitted additive candidates split the required properties: closed-face join is a categorical coproduct but idempotent with zero group completion, while geometric surface disjoint union preserves multiplicity but lacks coproduct injections and a universal property. Under explicit monoidal relaxation, additive N and Z follow, but no admitted multiplication candidate is simultaneously Carrier-level, coefficient-neutral, total unmarked, source-equivariant, unital, and distributive. Connected edge sewing has fixed-point deficit 1 and stable unit-arity residual 2; fixed-core regional products, all-even framed external products, and Brauer tensor live in coefficient/state sectors; the formal finite-family tensor is not source-admitted. The composed obstruction vector is (130,2,1,2). This closes the named inventory, not all future constructions. Phase I fails for the admitted inventory, so conditional Phase II is not authorized.",
