      "sent_at": "2026-08-20T18:51:42.045Z",
      "body": "Phase-I inventory closure is complete for every serious admitted candidate. Addition splits: face join is categorical but idempotent; surface disjoint union retains multiplicity but is only monoidal. Conditional additive N and Z are derivable, but 0/5 multiplication candidates are simultaneously Carrier-level, neutral, total unmarked, equivariant, unital, and distributive. Exact obstruction vector is (130 face-support excess, 2 missing coproduct legs, 1 sewing fixed-point deficit, 2 four-point unit arity residual). Fixed-core, framed all-even, and Brauer tensors are robust coefficient/state operations, not the common Carrier product; formal finite families are not source-derived. Packet/checker: research/grothendieck/phase-i-operation-inventory-closure.md and research/grothendieck/checkers/phase_i_operation_inventory_closure.py. This is scoped inventory closure, not global impossibility. Phase I does not pass, so Phase II remains unauthorized absent a new Carrier product/unit, component-inclusion coproduct structure, or explicit plan revision.",
      "entity_id": "maricicommunication:e830be117d1801a5d389"
    },
    {
      "op": "entity.declare",
      "local_ref": "msg_benincasa",
      "kind": "marici:communication",
      "title": "Grothendieck reports that the admitted inventory does not open Phase II",
      "sender": "marici.Grothendieck",
      "recipient": "marici.Benincasa",
      "intent": "result",
      "sent_at": "2026-08-20T18:51:42.045Z",
      "body": "Typed closure over the admitted inventory finds no Phase-I multiplication candidate: 0/5 pass Carrier level, neutrality, totality, equivariance, unit, and distributivity together. The all-even framed and Brauer products remain valid coefficient/state controls; the conditional surface monoid derives additive N and Z; neither yields the Carrier semiring. Exact obstruction vector is (130,2,1,2). Therefore the Burnside-Witt route remains gated under Nima's finalized plan. Packet: research/grothendieck/phase-i-operation-inventory-closure.md.",
